{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1858","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1858","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1858\",\"parent_revision\":\"90370f7a2f3fb849964e536de19af8ff1c99ec63\",\"root_revision\":\"a0c1873d8e0494e6aa858c4693ff80ba89b8da9192263ecef36b951084d65cd9\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Extract project conventions artifact and inject into task-worker delegation\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Create a small conventions extractor that distills CLAUDE.md and settings into a \u22642000-char artifact, registers it, and injects a reference into each task-worker delegation prompt.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. CLAUDE.md and rules/ location | AVAILABLE | /home/user/claude_skills/.claude/CLAUDE.md and .claude/rules/*.md \u2014 source documents\\n2. task-worker delegation prompt mechanism | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md \u2014 prompt template\\n3. implement-feature dispatch Step 2 | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md \u2014 step that builds delegation context\\n4. artifact_register for project-conventions type | AVAILABLE | backlog MCP artifact system supports new artifact types\\n5. Extract script design | DERIVABLE | filter criteria: exclude session behavior rules, session start/end hooks; retain technology choices, naming conventions, linting rules; condense to \u22642000 chars\\n6. Convention staleness / invalidation strategy | DERIVABLE | whether to re-extract per session vs. per issue vs. cache with hash check\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 implement path clear; extraction filter rules and invalidation strategy are design decisions to resolve in implementation.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **extract project conventions artifact and inject into task-worker delegation** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/agent-frameworks/orchestra.md \u2014 pattern: Project Convention Extraction (feature 9)\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-04-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] `uv run plugins/development-harness/scripts/extract_conventions.py --issue N` produces an artifact and registers it as type `project-conventions` for issue N\\n- [ ] `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"project-conventions\\\")` returns text \u22642000 characters containing repo convention substrings (e.g. `ruamel.yaml`, `uv run`)\\n- [ ] `implement-feature` Step 2 calls `extract_conventions.py` (or equivalent MCP tool) once per plan and appends the artifact reference to each `dh:task-worker` delegation prompt\\n- [ ] A spawned task-worker receives the conventions artifact content and uses it (verify by checking that a task body referencing `ruamel.yaml` does not produce a `pyyaml` import in the implementation)\\n- [ ] `uv run ty check plugins/development-harness/scripts/extract_conventions.py` \u2014 zero errors\\n- [ ] `uv run ruff check plugins/development-harness/scripts/extract_conventions.py` \u2014 zero errors\\n- [ ] `uv run pytest plugins/development-harness/tests/ -k conventions -x` passes (test: extractor output \u22642000 chars, contains `ruamel.yaml`, excludes `# Session Behavior` section headers)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/scripts/extract_conventions.py` (new) \u2014 PEP 723 script; reads CLAUDE.md + rules/*.md, filters and condenses to \u22642000 chars, artifact_registers result\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 Step 2 (add conventions extraction call)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/task-worker.md` \u2014 add conventions artifact reference to context-loading section\\n- `.claude/CLAUDE.md` and `.claude/rules/*.md` \u2014 source documents (read-only for this item)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_extract_conventions.py` (new) \u2014 unit tests\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs a **`dh:task-worker` subagent executing a SAM task**, I want **a distilled project conventions artifact injected into my delegation prompt** so that **I apply repo conventions (e.g. `ruamel.yaml` required, `pyyaml` banned, `uv run` not raw python) without needing every convention restated in each task body**.\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA new artifact type `project-conventions` registered via the artifact manifest. A small extractor (`plugins/development-harness/scripts/extract_conventions.py`) reads the repo's `.claude/CLAUDE.md`, `plugins/*/CLAUDE.md` in scope, and per-language settings (`pyproject.toml`, `package.json`), emits a distilled \u2264 2000-char markdown, and `artifact_register`s it at the parent issue. `implement-feature` Step 2 calls this extractor once and appends the artifact reference to each delegation prompt so `task-worker` reads it before executing.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- `uv run plugins/development-harness/scripts/extract_conventions.py --issue N` writes an artifact.\\n- `artifact_read(issue_number=N, artifact_type=\\\"project-conventions\\\")` returns text \u2264 2000 chars containing conventions substrings (e.g. `ruamel.yaml`).\\n- The string `\\\"# Session Behavior\\\"` (an example session-behavior header) is absent from the output \u2014 filtered as Orchestra's extractor does.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n`task-worker` loads whatever skills the task's `skills` field names and reads the task YAML \u2014 but receives no distilled project conventions. The harness relies on the orchestrator's own CLAUDE.md being loaded, which is a different address space from the subagent. Sub-agents therefore do not know that (for example) `ruamel.yaml` is required and `pyyaml` is banned, unless that rule appears inside the task body itself.\\n\\nGrep for `project-conventions`, `project_conventions`, or `extract.*conventions` across `plugins/development-harness/**` returns no hits \u2014 no code path produces such an artifact.\\n\\nSymptom: sub-agents violate repo conventions because they never received them. Repeated drift across sessions.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"5ef97b6d76c5911d9cd47a6a233f682ad561cac253f3c3ca95870d668266c139\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPtabsw\"}"}